WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.662 --> 00:00:01.688
- [Narrator] Tucked away
in the attic apartment

00:00:01.688 --> 00:00:05.194
of this nondescript Wichita
home, is a quixotic filmmaker.

00:00:05.194 --> 00:00:07.133
R.G. Miller is 53 year old auteur

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.928
who's making home movies with
the scope of blockbusters.

00:00:09.928 --> 00:00:11.589
And, when it comes to his self-described

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:13.804
Internet art films, R.G. does it all.

00:00:13.804 --> 00:00:15.529
- [R.G.] At RG Studios,
I'm the director,-

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:16.362
- Action.

00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:17.860
- [R.G.] the producer, the writer...

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.071
- [Narrator] The editor, the actor,

00:00:19.071 --> 00:00:21.229
the prop master, you name it.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:22.684
- [R.G.] I wear many hats.

00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:23.517
- [Narrator] He's been doing it that way

00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:26.057
for nearly 40 years,
with prolific results.

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:27.109
- Cut.

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:30.692
- [R.G.] All together,
I've made 46 films.

00:00:32.878 --> 00:00:35.795
(triumphant music)

00:00:37.671 --> 00:00:40.008
(screaming)

00:00:40.008 --> 00:00:41.299
- [Narrator] R.G.'s Internet art films,

00:00:41.299 --> 00:00:43.555
like any film, start with a script.

00:00:43.555 --> 00:00:45.541
- [R.G.] Like any film
coming out of Hollywood,

00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:47.029
a real good one, there has to be

00:00:47.029 --> 00:00:48.638
a little bit of yourself in there,

00:00:48.638 --> 00:00:51.084
or else what's the point?

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.302
That's where my storylines
for me come from.

00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:55.666
It's an expression within.

00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:59.833
For Hardliner it's the expressions
of dealing with society.

00:01:01.385 --> 00:01:03.174
- [Narrator] From there
it's on to prop, costume

00:01:03.174 --> 00:01:05.742
and set design, which R.G. 
handles in his own way.

00:01:05.742 --> 00:01:06.650
- [R.G.] You see over my shoulder,

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.385
you see chief back here, the boss.

00:01:08.385 --> 00:01:10.271
That was an old mask that I had.

00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:11.747
I cut it up and I started placing them,

00:01:11.747 --> 00:01:15.585
like you would a puzzle,
on a plastic bottle.

00:01:15.585 --> 00:01:18.681
That fit the description in my mind.

00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:21.492
I think that's kinda the voice I want.

00:01:21.492 --> 00:01:24.001
Whatever that takes by making whatever.

00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:25.501
What do you think?

00:01:27.069 --> 00:01:28.569
- Welcome to hell.

00:01:31.413 --> 00:01:32.919
- [Narrator] Next up, R.G.
gets into character

00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:35.036
by drawing inspiration from his life,

00:01:35.036 --> 00:01:37.304
including some of its darker moments.

00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:40.652
- [R.G.] I'm processing my
expressions, my emotions,

00:01:40.652 --> 00:01:43.735
my anger, my fits and my addictions.

00:01:46.122 --> 00:01:49.810
Trying to be perfect and flawless, Chief!

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.492
That's the illusion that we are under!

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:54.529
Don't you know this already?

00:01:54.529 --> 00:01:57.149
Making these films has replaced

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.153
the addiction that I once had.

00:01:59.153 --> 00:02:00.732
By coming here and making my studio,

00:02:00.732 --> 00:02:03.637
RG Studios, this is an addiction,

00:02:03.637 --> 00:02:07.205
but it's a process addiction,
because I'm examining it.

00:02:07.205 --> 00:02:08.691
I'm not allowing it to consume me,

00:02:08.691 --> 00:02:11.774
like I did the drugs and the alcohol.

00:02:15.053 --> 00:02:16.303
- [Narrator] Once the scene is shot,

00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:18.136
R.G. cuts together his vision.

00:02:18.136 --> 00:02:20.463
- For me, the best part of
making Internet art films

00:02:20.463 --> 00:02:24.213
is the actual process
of putting it together.

00:02:25.063 --> 00:02:25.934
- [Narrator] And the results are

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.684
unlike anything you've ever seen.

00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:34.113
- [R.G.] You're not supposed
to leave the crime scene.

00:02:34.113 --> 00:02:35.780
I was hungry, Chief!

00:02:38.022 --> 00:02:39.306
- [Narrator] Even after all his hard work,

00:02:39.306 --> 00:02:41.956
crowds aren't exactly
flocking to Miller's films.

00:02:41.956 --> 00:02:43.533
- I will probably get an average between

00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:45.590
two and three people
a week that will watch

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.597
something on my Internet YouTube channel.

00:02:48.597 --> 00:02:51.162
- [Narrator] Why keep doing
this with little to no audience?

00:02:51.162 --> 00:02:53.200
- [R.G.] For me, they are therapeutic.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.033
Ah phooey.

00:02:55.203 --> 00:02:59.062
My films allow me to examine my emotions.

00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:00.276
Once you examine something,

00:03:00.276 --> 00:03:03.384
you can edit out the
things that you don't like,

00:03:03.384 --> 00:03:05.253
or you can change the things

00:03:05.253 --> 00:03:09.420
that you have an opportunity
to change to your satisfaction.

00:03:11.446 --> 00:03:14.113
You did good, son, 
-Yes sir, commander
You did good.

